  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.90",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\Gamma$ be a graph of diameter $d$. For $i\\in\\{1,2,\\ldots,d\\}$, let $\\Gamma_i$ be the graph on the same vertex set as $\\Gamma$ with vertices $u,w$ adjacent in $\\Gamma_i$ if and only if $d_\\Gamma(u,w)=i$. Does there exist a $Q$-polynomial distance-regular graph $\\Gamma$ of diameter 3 such that $\\Gamma_2$ and $\\Gamma_3$ are strongly regular?",
